<body>

  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-ink-200/70 bg-white/85 backdrop-blur no-print">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 h-14 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <a href="<%= locals.protocal %><%= locals.domainName %>" class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-shrink-0">
        <img src="/images/logos/business.png" alt="COCOCE" class="h-12">
      </a>
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <a href="<%= locals.protocal %>business.<%= locals.domainName %>/dashboard" class="hidden sm:inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-xl text-xs font-medium text-ink-700 hover:bg-ink-100 transition" target="_blank">
          <i data-lucide="layout-dashboard" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
          Dashboard
        </a>
        <a href="<%= locals.protocal %>admin.<%= locals.domainName %>/dashboard" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-xl bg-brand text-white text-xs font-semibold hover:bg-brand-dark transition">
          <i data-lucide="shield-cog-corner" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
          Admin Dashboard
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-8 sm:pt-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand">Cookie Terms</p>
      <h1 class="mt-1 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink-900">
        Cookies we collect. How we correct them. How we use them.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink-500 leading-relaxed">
        This page explains what cookies COCOCE uses, how we keep them accurate and up to date,
        and exactly how they power the system's required and automated functionalities.
        We do not share your cookies with any third party.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs text-ink-400">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <i data-lucide="calendar" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i>
          Last updated: <%= locals.updatedAt || 'Latest' %>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <i data-lucide="globe" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i>
          Applies to all COCOCE platform services and sub-services 
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 sm:py-12 grid lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-8">

    <aside class="hidden lg:block no-print">
      <nav class="sticky top-20 text-sm" aria-label="On this page">
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold text-ink-400 mb-3">On this page</p>
        <ul class="space-y-0.5">
          <li><a href="#what-are-cookies" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">1. What are cookies</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cookies-we-collect" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">2. Cookies we collect</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-we-correct" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">3. How we correct them</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-we-use" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">4. How we use them</a></li>
          <li><a href="#no-third-party" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">5. No third-party sharing</a></li>
          <li><a href="#system-automated" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">6. System &amp; automated use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#your-control" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">7. Your control</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contact-cookies" class="toc-link block border-l-2 border-transparent pl-3 py-1.5 text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition">8. Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="prose-doc min-w-0">

      <section id="what-are-cookies">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">1. What are cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help
          the site remember your actions and preferences over time — such as keeping you signed
          in, remembering your display settings, and protecting against security threats.
        </p>
        <p>
          At COCOCE, we use cookies strictly for the operation of the marketplace and
          authentication system. We do not use them for advertising or tracking across other
          websites.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies-we-collect" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">2. Cookies we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect a minimal set of cookies, each with a clear and specific purpose:</p>

        <div class="space-y-4 mt-4">
          <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-3xl p-5 border border-[#e2edf7] shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand mb-3">
              <i data-lucide="key" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand"></i>
              Session Cookie (httpOnly, secure)
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-2">
              <strong>What it stores:</strong> A temporary session identifier that tells our
              servers you are logged in.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">
              <strong>Why we need it:</strong> Without this cookie, you would have to sign in
              again on every page you visit.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-3xl p-5 border border-[#e2edf7] shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand mb-3">
              <i data-lucide="user" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand"></i>
              Username Cookie
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-2">
              <strong>What it stores:</strong> Your display name or username, so the interface
              can greet you and personalize your experience.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">
              <strong>Why we need it:</strong> To remember who you are and display the correct
              account information without asking you repeatedly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-3xl p-5 border border-[#e2edf7] shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand mb-3">
              <i data-lucide="search" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand"></i>
              Search Index Cookie
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-2">
              <strong>What it stores:</strong> A lightweight index of your recent search queries
              and filters, used to speed up repeated searches.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">
              <strong>Why we need it:</strong> To provide faster, more relevant results and to
              remember your search context as you browse.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-3xl p-5 border border-[#e2edf7] shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand mb-3">
              <i data-lucide="shield-check" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand"></i>
              CSRF Protection Token
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-2">
              <strong>What it stores:</strong> A unique, unpredictable token tied to your session.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">
              <strong>Why we need it:</strong> To protect you from cross-site request forgery
              attacks — a common web security threat.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-3xl p-5 border border-[#e2edf7] shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand mb-3">
              <i data-lucide="sliders-horizontal" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand"></i>
              Preferences Cookie
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-2">
              <strong>What it stores:</strong> Your UI preferences, such as dark mode, language,
              and layout choices.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">
              <strong>Why we need it:</strong> To remember your settings so you don't have to
              reconfigure them on every visit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-correct" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">3. How we correct them</h2>
        <p>
          Cookie accuracy and integrity are important to us. Here is how we ensure the data
          stored in your cookies remains correct:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Automatic refresh:</strong> Session and CSRF tokens are regenerated on each sign-in and periodically during long sessions.</li>
          <li><strong>Validation checks:</strong> Every cookie is validated server-side before being trusted. Tampered or expired cookies are rejected immediately.</li>
          <li><strong>User-driven updates:</strong> When you change your username, preferences, or search filters, the associated cookies are updated in real time.</li>
          <li><strong>Cleanup on logout:</strong> All non-essential cookies are cleared when you sign out, ensuring no stale data remains.</li>
          <li><strong>Version tracking:</strong> Cookie formats carry a version marker. If we change the structure, old cookies are invalidated and refreshed automatically.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">4. How we use them</h2>
        <p>
          Every cookie we set serves one of the following purposes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> To verify that you are who you claim to be and to keep you signed in.</li>
          <li><strong>Security:</strong> To protect against CSRF, session hijacking, and other common web threats.</li>
          <li><strong>Personalization:</strong> To remember your display name, preferences, and search context.</li>
          <li><strong>Performance:</strong> To speed up search and navigation by caching lightweight indexes.</li>
          <li><strong>System requirements:</strong> To enable the platform's core, automated functionalities (see section 6).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use cookies for advertising, behavioral profiling, or cross-site tracking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="no-third-party" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">5. No third-party sharing</h2>
        <div class="bg-brand-light rounded-3xl p-5 md:p-6 border-l-4 border-brand flex items-center gap-4 shadow-sm my-4">
          <i data-lucide="shield-off" class="w-8 h-8 md:w-10 md:h-10 text-brand flex-shrink-0"></i>
          <div class="text-slate-800">
            <strong>We do not share your cookies with any third party.</strong> Not with
            advertisers, not with analytics providers, not with data brokers. Your cookie data
            stays within COCOCE's systems and is used solely for the purposes described on this
            page.
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          This means:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>No third-party tracking cookies are ever placed on your device by COCOCE.</li>
          <li>No cookie data is sold, rented, or traded to any external organization.</li>
          <li>No cookie data is shared with partners, affiliates, or service providers for their own use.</li>
          <li>All cookie processing happens on COCOCE-controlled infrastructure.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="system-automated" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">6. System &amp; automated use</h2>
        <p>
          Some cookies are essential for the system's required and automated functionalities.
          These include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Session continuity:</strong> Automatically maintaining your signed-in state as you navigate between pages.</li>
          <li><strong>Token refresh:</strong> Automatically renewing security tokens before they expire, so you are not interrupted.</li>
          <li><strong>Search indexing:</strong> Automatically caching your recent searches to deliver faster results on repeat queries.</li>
          <li><strong>Fraud detection:</strong> Automatically flagging suspicious cookie patterns that may indicate unauthorized access.</li>
          <li><strong>Load balancing:</strong> Automatically routing your requests to the appropriate server based on session affinity.</li>
          <li><strong>Preference persistence:</strong> Automatically applying your saved settings (theme, language, layout) on every visit.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These automated functions are what make COCOCE fast, secure, and reliable. They run
          in the background without requiring any action from you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-control" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">7. Your control</h2>
        <p>
          You have control over cookies at all times:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Browser settings:</strong> You can configure your browser to block or delete cookies. However, blocking essential cookies may prevent you from signing in or using core features.</li>
          <li><strong>Sign out:</strong> Signing out clears all non-essential cookies from your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Clear browsing data:</strong> You can manually clear cookies through your browser's settings at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Contact us:</strong> If you have questions about a specific cookie, reach out and we will explain exactly what it does.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact-cookies" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">8. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about cookies may be sent to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>General support — <a href="mailto:sales@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
          <li>Privacy matters — <a href="mailto:sales@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
          <li>Security concerns — <a href="mailto:sales@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-ink-200">
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-400">
          This document is provided for informational purposes and does not constitute legal
          advice. COCOCE recommends that users seek independent legal advice where appropriate.
          If anything here conflicts with mandatory law, the law prevails.
        </p>
      </section>

    </article>
  </div>

  <footer class="border-t border-ink-200 bg-white/60 no-print">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs text-ink-400">
      <span>© 2026 <span class="text-brand font-extrabold">COCOCE</span> — All right reserved.</span>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 justify-center">
        <a href="<%=locals.protocal%>auth.<%=locals.domainName%>/terms" target="_blank" class="hover:text-brand transition">Terms</a>
        <a href="<%=locals.protocal%>auth.<%=locals.domainName%>/privacy" target="_blank" class="hover:text-brand transition">Privacy</a>
        <a href="mailto:sales@cococe.rw" class="hover:text-brand transition">Support</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    lucide.createIcons();
  </script>
  <script src="/scripts/ck-terms.js"></script>

</body>

</html>